  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from Jul (590) to Aug (1180) and remain elevated in Sep (1260) (E-05). The best-supported mechanism: billing-config rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 with no unit scaling (E-13), misreads the 10x finer register resolution of firmware-v4.2 meters ('0.1 m3' vs legacy 'm3', E-14) as an abnormal consumption spike and rejects an otherwise valid, before-cutoff AMI read on billing import (REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION); this explains 1184 of 1240 (95.5%) disputed ESTIMATED-read bills (E-12). Whether this same defect, rather than a separate error, also drives the larger 59% share of disputes billed from ACTUAL reads (E-02) is not yet established."
